---
name: plan-critical-review-task
version: 1.0.0
description: assignment template for an agent-run critical plan review (critical-plan-reviewer role) during plan hardening.
format: xml
required_variables:
  - task_id
  - phase
  - branch
  - commit
  - worktree_path
  - round_index
  - review_focus
  - review_questions
  - references
optional_variables:
  - assignee
  - previous_step_json
defaults:
  assignee: "solar"
  previous_step_json: ""
metadata:
  type: plan-critical-review
  tags:
    - stage:plan
  workflow:
    scope:
      kind: phase
      variable: phase
    state: plan-critical-review
    stage: plan
    transition: critical-review
    iteration_variable: round_index
---
<atm-review id="{{ task_id }}" phase="{{ phase }}" assignee="{{ assignee }}" mode="plan-critical-review" round="{{ round_index }}">
  <branch>{{ branch }}</branch>
  <commit>{{ commit }}</commit>
  <worktree>{{ worktree_path }}</worktree>

  <review-focus>
{{ review_focus }}
  </review-focus>

  <review-questions>
{{ review_questions }}
  </review-questions>

  <references>
{{ references }}
  </references>

{% if previous_step_json | trim %}
  <previous-step-json>
<![CDATA[
{{ previous_step_json }}
]]>
  </previous-step-json>
{% endif %}

  <workflow>
    <step id="a">ACK this message immediately with `atm ack &lt;message-id&gt; "accepted {{ task_id }}: &lt;one line on what you do first&gt;"` (the message id is in the nudge line and the `atm read` header). The ack accepts the task; it does not close it.</step>
    <step id="b">Assume the `critical-plan-reviewer` role from `.claude/agents/critical-plan-reviewer.md`. Read every document in `<references>` from `{{ worktree_path }}` at commit `{{ commit }}` with `git show {{ commit }}:&lt;path&gt;`; never review working files.</step>
    <step id="c">Verify every claim the plan makes about existing code against the branch before recording a finding; cite `file:line` on `{{ commit }}`.</step>
    <step id="d">Return the STEP3 handoff fenced JSON (PLAN-CRIT-nnn findings, sprint_scores, PASS only at zero Blocking and zero Important) with `atm task close {{ task_id }} completed --stdin`.</step>
  </workflow>
</atm-review>
